      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "ab545780c1252d82de2db6def323cffd579afd6be5d1f70db05ffcb3bcea23e0"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "There are two ways by which the genotype of $x$ can be identical by descent with that of $y$: (1) the gene descending from $m_{x}$ may be identical by descent with that descending from $m_{y}$, and that from $f_{x}$ identical by descent with that from $f_{y}$, or (2) the gene from $m_{x}$ may be identical by descent with that from $f_{y}$, and that from $f_{x}$ identical by descent with that from $m_{y}$. Thus, the coefficient of fraternity is defined as",
      "source_page": 156,
      "printed_page": 136,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter7:p010:b6"
      ],
      "bbox": [
